<title>USA: Credit Store buys receivables.</title>
<headline>Credit Store buys receivables.</headline>
<dateline>SIOUX FALLS, S.D. 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Store Inc said Friday its Service One International Corp subsidiary acquired four debt and receivables portfolios.</p>
<p>The purchase, at substantial discounts, included about $600 million in defaulted credit card receivables and installment debt and approximately $15 million in outstanding credit card and &quot;past due&quot; receivables.</p>
<p>Service One is a national credit card service company specializing in the marketing, underwriting and administration of credit cards issued to sub-prime debtors.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
